		<preamble GUID="_57b13203-c2e5-4a51-b8a9-f66dc8e4cff5" eId="preamble">
			
			<formula GUID="_a8e5dcd4-4349-4132-a07a-9fd719b3aa59" eId="preamble__enactingWords" name="enactingText">
				<p>The Secretary of State makes these <ref class="placeholder" href="#varDocSubType"/> in exercise of the powers conferred by sections 3(5) and 166(1) of the Building Safety Act 2022<authorialNote GUID="_21e2a2d3-cea2-468b-a6c9-977369a22905" class="footnote" eId="fnote_1" marker="1">
						<p>2022 c. 30.</p>
					</authorialNote> and paragraph 24 of Schedule 1 to the Architects Act 1997<authorialNote GUID="_fe939b86-42a3-4c7e-8db5-e287df8e41f4" class="footnote" eId="fnote_10" marker="10">
						<p>1997 c. 22.</p>
					</authorialNote>.</p>
				<p>In respect of the provision at regulation 4, in accordance with section 7(4) of the Building Safety Act 2022 the Secretary of State has consulted the regulator<authorialNote GUID="_66cf0420-97de-473f-995c-1af2a8ec6452" class="footnote" eId="fnote_2" marker="2">
						<p>See section 2(1) of the Building Safety Act 2022 for the definition of “regulator” for the purposes of Part 2 of that Act.</p>
					</authorialNote> and such other persons as the Secretary of State considers appropriate.</p>
				<p>In respect of the provision at regulation 5, in accordance with paragraph 24(1) of Schedule 1 to the Architects Act 1997 the Secretary of State has consulted the Architects Registration Board and such other persons or bodies as the Secretary of State thinks fit.</p>
			</formula>
		</preamble>
		<body>
			
			<hcontainer GUID="_30d14c19-d3f1-4210-b5f3-2ef5c81fab97" class="prov1" eId="reg_1" name="regulation">
				
				<heading GUID="_cadd157b-1fec-4327-8f9b-650ad1f82b58" eId="reg_1__hdg">Citation, commencement and extent</heading>
				<num>1.</num>
				<paragraph GUID="_0b052043-a76d-4060-984a-dfa251cedfb6" class="prov2" eId="reg_1__para_1">
					<num>(1)</num>
					<content>
						<p>These Regulations may be cited as the Building Safety Act 2022 (Consequential Amendments and Prescribed Functions) and Architects Act 1997 (Amendment) Regulations 2023 and come into force on 1st April 2023.</p>
					</content>
				</paragraph>
				<paragraph GUID="_d049e325-e096-471d-8998-a2b980f552d8" class="prov2" eId="reg_1__para_2">
					<num>(2)</num>
					<content>
						<p>Subject to paragraph (3), these Regulations extend to England and Wales, Scotland and Northern Ireland.</p>
					</content>
				</paragraph>
				<paragraph GUID="_b209cbdb-fc62-473f-86ba-1ff949cea25d" class="prov2" eId="reg_1__para_3">
					<num>(3)</num>
					<content>
						<p>Regulation 4 extends to England and Wales.</p>
					</content>
				</paragraph>
			</hcontainer>
			<hcontainer GUID="_894988c3-e668-4476-9af6-b03108ef8a34" class="prov1" eId="reg_2" name="regulation">
				
				<heading GUID="_258caafe-89b7-4b29-8dc5-07e49bb6e552" eId="reg_2__hdg">Amendments to the Welsh Ministers (Transfer of Functions) (No. 2) Order 2009</heading>
				<num>2.</num>
				<paragraph GUID="_fe4c0ac7-52d1-476e-a943-7f9a5a3920d1" class="prov2" eId="reg_2__para_1">
					<num>(1)</num>
					<content>
						<p>The Welsh Ministers (Transfer of Functions) (No. 2) Order 2009<authorialNote GUID="_1bd88d73-d465-4327-807d-18b14de29942" class="footnote" eId="fnote_3" marker="3">
								<p>S.I. 2009/3019.</p>
							</authorialNote> is amended as follows.</p>
					</content>
				</paragraph>
				<paragraph GUID="_35ab3f29-965b-47d8-9ee8-ce58e1c529ad" class="prov2" eId="reg_2__para_2">
					<num>(2)</num>
					<content>
						<p>In article 8 (amendments to section 14 of the Building Act 1984: the Building Regulations Advisory Committee for England) omit paragraphs (2), (3) and (4).</p>
					</content>
				</paragraph>
				<paragraph GUID="_8f322f98-13bf-4bb3-ac2e-574473ea10e0" class="prov2" eId="reg_2__para_3">
					<num>(3)</num>
					<content>
						<p>Omit article 9 (transitional provision for members of the predecessor Building Regulations Advisory Committee).</p>
					</content>
				</paragraph>
				<paragraph GUID="_feb540a4-5bcb-437d-b6bf-ff696fdb8d30" class="prov2" eId="reg_2__para_4">
					<num>(4)</num>
					<content>
						<p>Omit article 10 (amendment to the Parliamentary Commissioner Act 1967 to refer to the Building Regulations Advisory Committee for England).</p>
					</content>
				</paragraph>
			</hcontainer>
			<hcontainer GUID="_937f79fb-5a84-46f6-b9a4-a96a7f498e7b" class="prov1" eId="reg_3" name="regulation">
				
				<heading GUID="_714182a7-ff49-484b-8a23-7379be491410" eId="reg_3__hdg">Amendment to the Freedom of Information (Additional Public Authorities) Order 2010</heading>
				<num>3.</num>
				<content>
					<p>In Part 2 of the Schedule to the Freedom of Information (Additional Public Authorities) Order 2010<authorialNote GUID="_95629dec-0752-4236-b9e4-ccefae4d0d55" class="footnote" eId="fnote_9" marker="9">
							<p>S.I. 2010/937.</p>
						</authorialNote>, omit the entry for the Building Regulations Advisory Committee for England.</p>
				</content>
			</hcontainer>
			<hcontainer GUID="_cd70d3ae-331c-427c-8db3-c93135a6db89" class="prov1" eId="reg_4" name="regulation">
				
				<heading GUID="_3ecb8b55-b3d5-42c5-ac80-eb287b05d217" eId="reg_4__hdg">Further functions of the regulator</heading>
				<num>4.</num>
				<intro GUID="_dbffca45-c717-45ec-9422-8589244469ae" eId="reg_4__intro">
					<p>For the purposes of section 3(5) of the Building Safety Act 2022, the functions of the Health and Safety Executive as statutory consultee in relation to the fire safety of higher-risk buildings or proposed higher-risk buildings under, or under any instrument made under—</p>
				</intro>
				<level GUID="_2759f21d-6ceb-4d6d-85c2-e80324ad5800" class="para1" eId="reg_4__para_a">
					<num>(a)</num>
					<content>
						<p>the Town and Country Planning Act 1990<authorialNote GUID="_eaad0909-e1b2-464d-9a9a-e3c011c6333c" class="footnote" eId="fnote_7" marker="7">
								<p>1990 c. 8.</p>
							</authorialNote>, and</p>
					</content>
				</level>
				<level GUID="_88dfac20-b4fb-46b6-ad82-b38a95bf78bb" class="para1" eId="reg_4__para_b">
					<num>(b)</num>
					<content>
						<p>section 54 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004<authorialNote GUID="_4bd8bd6a-6d34-4a8e-b527-6067f9e07b8c" class="footnote" eId="fnote_8" marker="8">
								<p>2004 c. 5.</p>
							</authorialNote>,</p>
					</content>
				</level>
				<wrapUp GUID="_7463cc48-dd8c-47e6-8802-f42934b9e367" eId="reg_4__wrapup">
					<p>are prescribed as functions of the regulator.</p>
				</wrapUp>
			</hcontainer>
			<hcontainer GUID="_fe0bb636-13a5-424e-a2fe-7e0fcf21ea74" class="prov1" eId="reg_5" name="regulation">
				
				<heading GUID="_e8ecaad8-dbc7-412d-b9fd-a98bf5067205" eId="reg_5__hdg">Amendment to the Architects Act 1997</heading>
				<num>5.</num>
				<intro GUID="_d24ec03b-47b5-4f86-947b-9f61b719ef8d" eId="reg_5__intro">
					<p>In Schedule 1 to the Architects Act 1997, omit paragraph 20.</p>
				</intro>
				<level GUID="_ab2e02c3-27c3-4ee1-968f-545606dddf2a" class="unnumberedParagraph" eId="reg_5__para">
					<content>
						
					</content>
				</level>
				<level GUID="_24e694e1-d1b0-44ee-8250-a5ff58f7f2b3" class="unnumberedParagraph" eId="reg_5__para__oc_1">
					<content>
						
					</content>
				</level>
			</hcontainer>
			<hcontainer GUID="_2dfcc8f5-d73d-4327-8691-037bda150520" eId="sigs" name="signatures">
				
				<hcontainer GUID="_045d7f3d-aaec-40bd-8ee2-3ae0b3fef6ab" eId="sigs__sigBlk" name="signatureBlock">
					<content>
						<p>Signed by authority of the Secretary of State for Levelling Up, Housing and Communities</p>
						<block GUID="_0ed2431d-3e8e-48cf-84ef-9d4457831b53" eId="sigs__sigBlk__sig" name="signature">Lee Rowley</block>
						<block GUID="_0b159326-7d57-4da3-b7aa-bb7fc4851e1d" eId="sigs__sigBlk__role" name="role">Parliamentary Under Secretary of State</block>
						<block name="date"><date date="2023-02-27">27th February 2023</date></block>
						<block GUID="_6d67f709-d9cb-4e31-826f-454d8106fb4d" eId="sigs__sigBlk__org" name="organization">Department for Levelling Up, Housing and Communities</block>
					</content>
				</hcontainer>
			</hcontainer>
		</body>
		<conclusions GUID="_c76ac26a-59f0-43b1-a56b-428c23a66dae" eId="backCover">
			
			<blockContainer GUID="_264a60a8-d8d3-4c22-bf11-28080765b65f" class="explanatoryNote" eId="backCover__explNote">
				<heading GUID="_179b08f9-a449-4062-ae55-9ccede53e8f9" eId="backCover__explNote__hdg">Explanatory Note</heading>
				<subheading GUID="_6ea9a94e-1c44-4a31-a3e0-792d337a9641" eId="backCover__explNote__subhdg">(This note is not part of the <ref class="placeholder" href="#varDocSubType"/>)</subheading>
				<p>Section 9(3) of the Building Safety Act 2022 (c. 30) abolishes the Building Regulations Advisory Committee for England. The Building Regulations Advisory Committee for Wales will remain. Regulations 2 and 3 of these Regulations consequentially remove references to the Building Regulations Advisory Committee for England.</p>
				<p>Regulation 4 prescribes as functions of the regulator, the Health and Safety Executive (“HSE”), certain functions of HSE as statutory consultee under town and country planning legislation. These are added to the functions of the regulator under or by virtue of the Building Act 1984 (c. 55) or the Building Safety Act 2022 to include them in the meaning of “building function” in Part 2 of the Building Safety Act 2022.</p>
				<p>Regulation 5 amends Schedule 1 to the Architects Act 1997 to omit paragraph 20. The amendment is a consequence of amendments made to paragraph 19 of that Schedule by the Architects (Fees, Electronic Communications and Miscellaneous Amendments) Regulations 2022, S.I. 2022/1388.</p>
				<p>An impact assessment has not been produced for this instrument as no, or no significant, impact on the private, voluntary or public sector is foreseen.</p>
			</blockContainer>
		</conclusions>
	</act>
